message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **interactive card** that rotates (spins) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** – no JavaScript required.

---

## 1️⃣ Markup (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">   <!-- or <style>…</style> -->
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Here’s the back side content.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

* `card-wrapper` keeps the card centered and provides perspective.  
* Inside we have two faces: `.card-front` and `.card-back`.  

---

## 2️⃣ Styling (CSS)

```css
/* ------------- General reset & layout ---------------- */
body {
    margin: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    background: #f0f0f0;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

/* ------------- Card container ------------------------ */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;          /* card width */
    height: 200px;         /* card height */
    perspective: 800px;    /* gives depth to 3D transform */
}

/* ------------- Card itself --------------------------- */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* smooth rotation */
}

/* ------------- Hover effect -------------------------- */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* rotate 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ------------- Card faces ---------------------------- */
.card > div {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

.card-front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
    color: #333;
}

.card-back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a18cd1 0%, #fbc2eb 100%);
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);      /* start flipped so it shows on hover */
}
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | The `.card-wrapper` sets a **perspective** so 3D transforms look realistic. |
| 2 | The `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3D space. |
| 3 | On hover, the `.card` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis (`rotateY(180deg)`), flipping it. |
| 4 | Each face (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) is absolutely positioned and covers the whole card. |
| 5 | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 6 | The back face starts already rotated 180°, so it becomes visible after the card flips. |

---

## 🎨 Customization Tips

| Property | What to tweak | Example |
|----------|---------------|---------|
| `width / height` | Size of the card | `width: 350px; height: 250px;` |
| `perspective` | Depth effect | `perspective: 1200px;` |
| `transition` | Speed & easing | `transition: transform 1s cubic-bezier(.25,.46,.45,.94);` |
| `background` | Color scheme | Use gradients, images, or solid colors. |
| `border-radius` | Rounded corners | `border-radius: 20px;` |
| `box-shadow` | Shadow style | `box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);` |

Feel free to copy the code into your project and adjust the values to match your design. Happy coding!
